leading models like YOLOv8 and Roboflow 3.0, which showed lower mAP, precision, and recall values under similar conditions. Additionally, while models such as Fmask-RCNN and MobileNetV2 exhibit high training accuracy, they lack the real-time assessment capabilities critical for port applications, making YOLO-NAS a more suitable choice. The successful integration of YOLO-NAS for automated container damage detection has significant implications for the logistics industry, enhancing port operations with reliable, real-time inspection solutions that can seamlessly integrate into predictive maintenance and monitoring systems. This approach reduces operational costs, improves safety, and lessens the reliance on manual inspections, contributing to the development of \\"smart ports\\" with higher efficiency and sustainability in container management.", "作者": ["Thanh Nguyen Thi Phuong", "Gyu-Sung Cho", "Indranath Chatterjee"], "年份": 2025, "发表位置": "Science Progress"}}'}], 'model': 'DeepSeek-V4-Flash[free]', 'max_tokens': 4000, 'reasoning_effort': 'none', 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0}} | ctx={"client_host": "127.0.0.1", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/sessions/14f48db5cf134862b21b1a82743b6e42/runs", "run_id": "run_7b82e6fa0a2141fdbae4810c95e01a6d", "session_key": "14f48db5cf134862b21b1a82743b6e42", "turn_id": "3fc9d442-2867-40df-89d0-77fa4801b454"}
