o collect images of the five sides of the automobile synchronously. Then the AIS extracts candidate defect regions from the vehicle body image by a multi-scale Hessian matrix fusion method. Finally, candidate defect regions are classified into pseudo-defects, dents and scratches by feature extraction (shape, size, statistics and divergence features) and a support vector machine algorithm. Experimental results demonstrate that automatic inspection system can effectively reduce false detection of pseudo-defects produced by image noise and achieve accuracies of 95.6% in dent defects and 97.1% in scratch defects, which is suitable for customs inspection of imported vehicles.", "作者": ["Qinbang Zhou", "Renwen Chen", "Bin Huang", "Chuan Liu", "Jie Yu", "Xiaoqing Yu"], "年份": 2019, "发表位置": "Sensors"}}'}], 'model': 'DeepSeek-V4-Flash[free]', 'max_tokens': 4000, 'reasoning_effort': 'none', 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0}} | ctx={"client_host": "127.0.0.1", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/sessions/14f48db5cf134862b21b1a82743b6e42/runs", "run_id": "run_7b82e6fa0a2141fdbae4810c95e01a6d", "session_key": "14f48db5cf134862b21b1a82743b6e42", "turn_id": "3fc9d442-2867-40df-89d0-77fa4801b454"}
